    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8477580-customer-engagement-lead": {
      "title": "Customer Engagement Lead",
      "description": "Customer Engagement Lead - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Customer Engagement Lead Shape how IESE connects with candidates, participants and alumni through smarter journeys, meaningful insights and impactful communication across channels. Apply for this job The Customer Engagement Lead will be responsible for helping IESE evolve the way it engages with candidates, participants and Alumni across its commercial communication channels. The role will act as the bridge between business teams, customer data and Customer Engagement platforms , ensuring that communication initiatives are relevant, coordinated, measurable and aligned with business priorities. This position combines business partnering, Customer Engagement, Marketing Automation and analytics , working closely with Marketing, Programs, Data & AI and external technology partners. Key responsibilities Business partnering and Customer Engagement strategy. Work closely with Marketing, Programs and other business areas to understand their objectives, identify opportunities and translate business needs into Customer Engagement initiatives, communication strategies and actionable plans. Customer journeys, segmentation and personalization. Lead the functional evolution of customer journeys and communication approaches, promoting better use of customer data, preferences, interests and behavior to deliver more relevant and personalized interactions across channels. Communication governance and coordination. Coordinate communication activity across business areas, audiences and channels, helping establish priorities, manage overlaps and communication pressure, and ensure a consistent customer experience. Performance and analytics. Use data to evaluate the effectiveness of campaigns, journeys and customer interactions, define relevant KPIs and translate insights into concrete recommendations to improve engagement, conversion and business outcomes. Functional ownership and external delivery. Define functional requirements and coordinate the external partners responsible for the technical operation of Customer Engagement platforms, prioritizing the backlog, following up delivery and ensuring that solutions meet business needs and quality expectations. Continuous improvement and innovation. Act as an internal reference for Customer Engagement best practices, challenging existing processes and legacy approaches, identifying opportunities for simplification and automation, promoting common standards and exploring new capabilities and use cases. The role will retain the internal functional ownership of Customer Engagement , while the recurring technical configuration and operation of the platforms will primarily be delivered by external partners. The position will also contribute to the evolution of IESE’s Customer Engagement ecosystem, ensuring that current initiatives remain scalable and supporting future changes in CRM and Marketing Automation technologies. Requirements Bachelor’s Degree in Business, Marketing, Engineering, Data, Economics or a related field. 5+ years of experience in Customer Engagement, Marketing Automation, CRM, Digital Marketing or related roles. Experience working directly with business stakeholders and translating business objectives into functional solutions. Strong understanding of customer journeys, segmentation, personalization and digital communication strategies. Solid analytical skills and experience working with engagement, marketing and conversion KPIs. Ability to interpret data and turn insights into practical business recommendations. Experience coordinating external providers, agencies or technical delivery teams. Experience working in cross-functional environments with multiple stakeholders. Professional working proficiency in English and Spanish. Highly valued Experience with Salesforce Marketing Cloud Account Engagement / Pardot, Salesforce, Brevo or similar Customer Engagement platforms. Experience with reporting and visualization tools such as Power BI. Understanding of CRM and customer data models. Experience with lead nurturing, scoring, attribution or personalization. Experience managing email, WhatsApp or other digital communication channels. Experience in organizations with multiple business units and complex or long customer decision journeys. Competencies Strong business and customer orientation. Analytical and data-driven mindset. Stakeholder management and communication skills. Ability to challenge the status quo constructively. Strategic thinking combined with a hands-on delivery mindset. Prioritization and decision-making. Cross-functional collaboration. Proactivity, autonomy and ownership. Continuous improvement mindset. Location Barcelona, Spain Remote status Hybrid Employment type Full-time Apply for this job Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Customer Engagement Lead Shape how IESE connects with candidates, participants and alumni through smarter journeys, meaningful insights and impactful communication across channels. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8428800-business-development-manager-iese-publishing": {
      "title": "Business Development Manager",
      "description": "Business Development Manager - IESE Publishing - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Business Development Manager - IESE Publishing Expand IESE Publishing’s global reach by opening markets, building lasting partnerships and shaping learning solutions, with Latin America and Spain at the heart of your international remit. Apply for this job Help expand the international reach of IESE knowledge and learning solutions. IESE Publishing is looking for an experienced Business Development Manager to drive growth, open new markets and build long-term relationships with academic institutions, companies and partners around the world. Latin America is a priority market and requires regular travel, with Spain also a key focus. At the same time, the role has a genuinely international remit: the successful candidate will be expected to identify and develop opportunities in other high-potential markets, using both in-person and remote approaches depending on the opportunity. The role: This is a hands-on business development role combining new market development, B2B sales, strategic account management, faculty engagement and market intelligence. The person will develop new clients while growing existing accounts, understand what customers need, and connect those needs with IESE Publishing materials, digital formats and learning solutions. The role works closely with the Director of IESE Publishing and the rest of the team to turn market insight into commercial opportunities and, when needed, into new solutions. Key responsibilities: Market and business development: Develop and execute commercial activity across priority markets, segments and channels, with Latin America as a key focus, Spain as another priority market, and active exploration of opportunities in other geographies. Prospect and develop new clients across business schools, universities, other academic institutions, companies, Corporate Universities and other relevant segments. Travel regularly, particularly across Latin America and Spain, to open new accounts, strengthen relationships with recurring clients, understand needs first-hand and identify new opportunities. Develop opportunities in other international markets through videoconferences, digital outreach, partners and other channels when travel is not required or not yet justified. Contribute to the development of new distributors, partners, channels and other routes to market that can extend the reach of IESE Publishing and IESE content. Clients, solutions and relationships: Build and grow long-term relationships with academic institutions, companies, partners and strategic accounts, engaging with academic leaders and faculty as well as executives, HR, Learning & Development and procurement teams. Understand each client's needs and present the materials, formats and learning solutions that best respond to them, including interactive and digital solutions. Develop and negotiate tailored commercial proposals when appropriate, including licenses, annual packs, certification and other solutions for academic and corporate clients. Collaborate with other commercial divisions at IESE, Program Directors, Faculty and other relevant areas to identify opportunities, facilitate contacts and shape solutions when needed. Faculty engagement, events and outreach: Represent IESE Publishing at relevant fairs, conferences, events and academic forums to generate leads, develop relationships and strengthen market visibility. During visits to schools and universities, actively meet professors and academic teams to present new materials, formats and possibilities and to understand their teaching needs. Design, organize and deliver seminars and webinars on the case method, IESE Publishing materials, new formats and learning solutions, working with IESE faculty when appropriate. Sales discipline and market intelligence: Maintain complete and accurate commercial information in Salesforce, including accounts, contacts, meetings, visits, opportunities, next steps and sales funnel stages, ensuring a reliable pipeline and forecast. Document and report business trips and client visits, including contacts made, needs and opportunities identified, conclusions, follow-up actions and next steps. Use IESE Publishing's Business Intelligence, distributor reports, Salesforce and other relevant sources to identify markets, institutions, clients, segments or materials with growth potential. Bring market and client insight back to the team so that IESE Publishing can anticipate needs, decide what to promote or improve, and co-create new services or commercial models when appropriate. Candidate profile: Bachelor's degree in Business, Marketing, Sales or a related field; MBA or Master's degree is a plus. At least 5 years of relevant experience in Business Development, B2B sales or strategic account development, with a proven track record of opening business and growing long-term client relationships. Experience in education, executive education, publishing, learning solutions or a related sector is highly valued. Strong communication and relationship-building skills, with confidence engaging senior decision-makers, academic leaders and faculty. Strong analytical skills and disciplined use of CRM and data; experience with Salesforce is particularly valuable. Fluency in Spanish and English is required; additional languages are an advantage. Availability and willingness to travel regularly, especially within Latin America and Spain. What will make you succesful: We are looking for someone commercially ambitious, curious and highly relationship-oriented: a person who enjoys opening doors, travelling, meeting clients and faculty, and building trust over time. The role also requires rigor: opportunities must be followed through the funnel, market signals must be translated into action, and data must be used alongside personal relationships and judgment. An interest in education and in how learning is evolving will be a strong asset. This is an opportunity to play a central role in the international growth of IESE Publishing and in extending the reach and impact of IESE knowledge worldwide. Location Barcelona, Spain Remote status Hybrid Apply for this job Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Business Development Manager - IESE Publishing Expand IESE Publishing’s global reach by opening markets, building lasting partnerships and shaping learning solutions, with Latin America and Spain at the heart of your international remit. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8367288-mim-mif-admissions-coordinator": {
      "title": "MIM & MIF Admissions Coordinator",
      "description": "MIM & MIF Admissions Coordinator - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Madrid, Spain · Hybrid MIM & MIF Admissions Coordinator Support global MiM & MiF admissions by nurturing candidates, coordinating events and interviews, and creating seamless experiences in a collaborative international team. Apply for this job The MIM & MIF Admissions Coordinator Mission is to actively support the MiM / MiF Admissions team in the commercial and recruitment activities, facilitating the attraction, engagement, and conversion of high-caliber international candidates for the MiM and MiF programs. The coordinator acts as a vital commercial partner, managing lead nurturing processes and optimizing administrative workflows to accelerate candidate enrollment and achieve intake targets. Key Responsibilities Liaise with Associate Directors to coordinate regional recruitment events, corporate info sessions, and national and international school fairs. Nurture incoming leads and inquiries (warm prospects) through targeted email campaigns and proactive follow-ups to convert initial interest into submitted applications. Prepare regional pipeline summaries and competitor analysis reports for the commercial team to identify recruitment opportunities and support strategic decision-making. Act as the primary operational support for Associate Directors during corporate presentations and high-priority networking events. Monitor and track candidate progression through the CRM system, identifying bottlenecks in the pipeline to accelerate the admissions decision process. Validate submitted application portfolios, ensuring all compliance and qualification benchmarks are met before presenting files to the Admissions Committee. Orchestrate scheduling logistics for admissions interviews, matching global candidates with faculty, admissions directors, and alumni across multiple time zones Coordinate operational logistics for both virtual and on-campus admissions events (such as Open Houses, Info Sessions, and Assessment Days) to deliver a premium brand experience Manage the preparation and distribution of admissions welcome packets, orientation schedules, and enrollment collateral for new intakes Requirements Bachelor's degree. 2 to 3 years of experience in Premium Customer Success or Sales, Hospitality & Event Operations or Higher Education / Student Affairs. CRM Database Experience: Salesforce, Dynamics… Strong service orientation and commitment to delivering an exceptional participant experience. Ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders in a collaborative and international environment. High attention to detail and strong problem-solving capabilities. Excellent communication skills in English and Spanish, both written and spoken. Strong digital skills and experience using information systems and Microsoft Office applications. Proactive mindset with a continuous improvement orientation and the ability to work autonomously. Location Madrid, Spain Remote status Hybrid Apply for this job Madrid, Spain · Hybrid MIM & MIF Admissions Coordinator Support global MiM & MiF admissions by nurturing candidates, coordinating events and interviews, and creating seamless experiences in a collaborative international team. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8355114-campus-operations-unit-coordinator-temporary": {
      "title": "Campus Operations Unit Coordinator (Temporary)",
      "description": "Campus Operations Unit Coordinator (Temporary) - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Campus Operations Unit Coordinator (Temporary) Coordina la logística y los servicios del campus para ofrecer experiencias excelentes a participantes y equipos, resolviendo retos con iniciativa, organización y orientación al detalle. Apply for this job (Duración aproximada hasta Marzo 2027) 1. Responsabilidades: Tiene la misión de llevar a cabo la logística y coordinación de la gestión de programas del IESE, ofreciendo un excelente servicio a los clientes internos y participantes de programas. Sus funciones principales son: Asesorar, colaborar, tramitar y supervisar las operaciones necesarias (logística, restauración, audiovisuales, limpieza, parquing, mantenimiento, etc.) para el buen desarrollo de las distintas actividades y programas de la escuela. Gestión de solicitudes, incidencias y resoluciones del personal interno en temas relacionados con reserva de espacios, material, mensajería, comedor, mantenimiento, seguridad, etc. Coordinación para la optimización de instalaciones y servicios. Atención telefónica a los clientes internos. 2. Perfil Candidato: Grado o Secretariado de dirección. Experiencia previa de un mínimo de dos años en tareas de gestión de eventos. Dominio de ofimática (Outlook, Excel, Power Point). Inglés nivel avanzado. 3. Requerimientos: Orientación al cliente (interno): responder con prontitud ante las demandas y sugerencias de sus clientes; actúa pensando en las necesidades reales de los clientes; establece y mantiene relaciones efectivas y se sabe ganar el respeto y confianza de los clientes. Trabajo en equipo: trabaja de forma coordinada con el resto del equipo. Sentido de pertenencia y propósito compartido. Gestión de recursos: conoce los objetivos y analiza con detenimiento cuál es el modo más eficiente de alcanzarlos; tiene en cuenta los posibles usos alternativos de los recursos teniendo en cuenta su rentabilidad; cumple el presupuesto aprobado para cada proyecto. Proactividad: iniciativa, creatividad y optimismo. Toma la dirección de los problemas y está encima de ellos hasta que se han resuelto; responde con un apropiado nivel de urgencia; promueve frecuentemente mejora en su departamento. Organización y priorización: sabe gestionar y coordinar esfuerzos para alcanzar los objetivos a corto plazo; analiza la información para ser capaz de priorizar. Orientación a la mejora continua y al cuidado del detalle. Capacidad para entender distintas perspectivas y serenidad en entornos exigentes. Location Barcelona, Spain Remote status Hybrid Employment type Full-time Apply for this job Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Campus Operations Unit Coordinator (Temporary) Coordina la logística y los servicios del campus para ofrecer experiencias excelentes a participantes y equipos, resolviendo retos con iniciativa, organización y orientación al detalle. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
