    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8324986-a-research-assistant-to-run-the-behavioral-lab": {
      "title": "A Research Assistant to run the Behavioral Lab",
      "description": "A Research Assistant to run the Behavioral Lab - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Research Assistants · Barcelona, Spain · Onsite A Research Assistant to run the Behavioral Lab Apply for this job You will have two primary responsibilities: (1) Your primary role will be to oversee the daily research being conducted in IESE’s Behavioral Lab, including scheduling and running of online or in-lab studies. developing and maintaining the participant pool, programming surveys and experiments, completing Internal Review Board (IRB) submissions, etc. (2) Work with faculty and PhD students from different departments within IESE Business School to conduct a diverse set of research studies. The research being conducted spans many topics, including decision-making, behavioral economics and finance, consumer and organizational behavior. You will be trained on the latest integration of AI in research methods and be expected to support faculty research using AI. You will report to the Academic Lab Director and the Research Centers and Activities Director. Responsibilities Schedule and supervise the running of online and in-lab studies. Manage online survey panel deployment for researchers. Create and maintain a pool for lab-based and online studies (posting and approving studies, recruiting participants, …) Assist researchers with experiment design, data collection, and analysis Submit and approve participants payment requests Facilitate and coordinate the day-to-day operations Provide support to participants and researchers Provide support in other activities of professors (related to experiments) Engage with AI agents to support academic research Requirements Work-permit in Spain · Undergraduate or post-graduate degree in psychology, psychological research or related fields, such as consumer behavior, organizational behavior, statistics, economics, or other scientific methodology · Experience designing experimental behavioral research studies · Very good organization and attention to detail · Excellent social and communication skills · Working knowledge of AI platforms like ChatGPT/Codex and Anthropic/Claude Full fluency in English at a native level or equivalent. Excellent English writing skills. Conditions Full-time position 1830 euros / months before tax Start date ASAP End date 1 year with the possibility of extending. Department Research Assistants Location Barcelona, Spain Employment type Full-time Apply for this job Research Assistants · Barcelona, Spain · Onsite A Research Assistant to run the Behavioral Lab Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8302919-data-engineer": {
      "title": "Data Engineer",
      "description": "Data Engineer - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Data Engineer Construye pipelines y modelos de datos robustos con Azure Data Factory, dbt y Snowflake, impulsando decisiones de negocio con calidad, autonomía y propósito. Apply for this job Misión del rol El rol de Data Engineer es eminentemente técnico y de ejecución. Buscamos a alguien que disfrute escribiendo código, construyendo pipelines robustos y resolviendo con velocidad las necesidades cambiantes del negocio. El Data Engineer será el propietario técnico de Azure Data Factory (ADF) y dbt — las herramientas que dan vida al Data Lake de Snowflake — y será la pieza que permite al equipo moverse rápido sin romper nada. Su trabajo se mide en entregas reales: ETLs que funcionan, modelos que reflejan el negocio, y datos que llegan limpios y a tiempo a quien los necesita. Responsabilidades principales Transformación y modelado de datos (dbt) Ser el referente técnico de dbt en el equipo: diseño de modelos, capas Staging / Intermediate / Mart, tests de calidad y documentación. Desarrollar y mantener los modelos Silver y Gold del Data Lake en coordinación con los responsables de dominio de datos. Establecer y hacer cumplir las convenciones de desarrollo (naming, lineage, testing, materialización). Integrar dbt con las herramientas de observabilidad y gobierno del dato existentes. Contribuir a la arquitectura y roadmap del Dataplatform. Ingestión y orquestación (Azure Data Factory) Ser el owner técnico de los pipelines de ADF: diseño, despliegue, monitorización y resolución de incidencias. Gestionar la ingestión desde los sistemas fuente actuales (ERP, CRM, herramientas de Marketing, etc.) hacia la capa Bronze/Silver de Snowflake. Optimizar el rendimiento y coste de los pipelines existentes y diseñar los nuevos a medida que el scope crece. Calidad, Gobierno y colaboración Aplicar una mentalidad Data Governance first : naming, linaje, clasificación y trazabilidad forman parte del trabajo, no son un paso posterior. Trabajar codo con codo con analistas de BI, marketing automation y el AI Taskforce para garantizar que el dato llega a tiempo y en condiciones. Actuar como contraparte técnica del proveedor externo de plataforma, velando por la coherencia y calidad de las entregas. Contribuir a una cultura de calidad del dato: tests automatizados, documentación, linaje, e identificación de problemas para su tratamiento con los data stewards. Mantener el catálogo de datos actualizado y apoyar al equipo de Governance en la evolución de los activos. Mantener y evolucionar el framework de seguridad actual Aplicar políticas de seguridad y enmascaramiento de datos para asegurar su privacidad y buen uso. Perfil técnico requerido Imprescindible Experiencia demostrable con dbt Core o dbt Cloud en entornos productivos (2+ años). Conocimiento sólido de Azure Data Factory: pipelines, triggers, linked services, Integration Runtimes. Dominio de SQL avanzado y experiencia con Snowflake o plataformas cloud similares (BigQuery, Redshift). Familiaridad con patrones de arquitectura de datos: Medallion (Bronze/Silver/Gold), Data Vault, dimensional modeling. Experiencia con Git y flujos de trabajo CI/CD para proyectos de datos. Valorable Conocimiento de Python para tareas de ingeniería de datos (PySpark, Pandas, scripts de automatización). Experiencia con plataformas de gobierno del dato o catálogos, en dbt Semantic Layers Familiaridad con Power BI o herramientas de BI modernas como consumidores de las capas de datos. Conocimiento de herramientas de IA/ML en el contexto del dato (MLflow, Feature Stores, etc.). Experiencia en herramientas tipo Ask Your Data. Perfil personal Orientación al ownership: capaz de llevar un dominio técnico de principio a fin, con autonomía, integridad y sentido de responsabilidad. Espíritu de servicio: entiende que su trabajo existe para que otros puedan tomar mejores decisiones. El dato es un medio; las personas, el fin. Excelencia y mejora continua: propone estándares, documenta, y no deja deuda técnica sin gestionar. Comunicación clara con perfiles no técnicos: sabe traducir decisiones de ingeniería a lenguaje de negocio. Trabajo en equipo en entornos pequeños y ágiles, con exposición directa a la dirección. Adaptabilidad a un entorno en construcción: sin miedo a la hoja en blanco ni a tomar decisiones con información incompleta. Location Barcelona, Spain Remote status Hybrid Employment type Full-time Apply for this job Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Data Engineer Construye pipelines y modelos de datos robustos con Azure Data Factory, dbt y Snowflake, impulsando decisiones de negocio con calidad, autonomía y propósito. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8108580-research-assistant-to-prof-xavier-vives": {
      "title": "Research Assistant to Prof. Xavier Vives",
      "description": "Research Assistant to Prof. Xavier Vives - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Research Assistants · Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Research Assistant to Prof. Xavier Vives Join Prof. Xavier Vives' team as a Research Assistant: contribute to cutting-edge economics research (IO, digital economies, finance), develop data, modeling, and policy skills... Apply for this job As a research assistant, you will have the opportunity to participate in all aspects of the research process (on topics covering industrial organization, digital economies, financial markets and banking) including literature search and review, theoretical analysis, model simulation, data collection, and research design. Requirements: BS/Ba in Economics. Master in Economics or Finance and policy interest valued. Knowledge in LaTex/Scientific Word, Matlab, R, Python, Mathematica, Stata valued Work-permit in Spain High level command of English and excellent writing skills in English and Spanish (Catalan valued) Students finalizing a BS/Ba in Economics with strong record or a Master Degree are welcome Students envisaging to pursue an Economic or Business PhD are also welcome Conditions: Full-time position 1.830€ month before tax Department Research Assistants Location Barcelona, Spain Remote status Hybrid Employment type Full-time Apply for this job Research Assistants · Barcelona, Spain · Hybrid Research Assistant to Prof. Xavier Vives Join Prof. Xavier Vives' team as a Research Assistant: contribute to cutting-edge economics research (IO, digital economies, finance), develop data, modeling, and policy skills... Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/107460": {
      "title": "Full-time Post-Doc Position for the Puig Chair of Global Leadership Development at IESE Business School",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School Location: Barcelona, Spain The Post-Doc Position The Puig Chair of Global Leadership Development at IESE Business School invites applications for a three-year Post-Doctoral position. The primary criterion for acceptance is research excellence in the field of Organizational Behavior/Strategic Leadership and an interest in studying topics related to Top Management Teams, leadership development, and employee well-being. Ideally the candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline. The position will start ideally by September 2022; candidates should have finished their Ph.D. degree by the start date. This position will be responsible for conducting original research with the Chairholder Prof. Anneloes Raes, who will supervise the candidate’s work. This position is also expected to become actively involved in the IESE Business School intellectual communities by regularly participating in research seminars, brown bag presentations, etc. Teaching is not required. Research Topics Top management team impact on organizations Strategic leadership and employee well-being Leadership development The interface of top management team and middle managers IESE Business School IESE Business School (www.iese.edu) is the Graduate School of Management of the University of Navarra, with main campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York and Sao Paulo. It offers master-level (Master in Business Administration), graduate (Ph.D. in management), and executive education programs. Founded in 1958, recent rankings of the Financial Times, the Economist, and Business Week consistently situate IESE among the top-5 business schools in Europe. With full-time professors from 25 countries and professors with PhDs from the world’s leading universities, the faculty’s teaching and research efforts are global in outlook and content. IESE has about 32.000 alumni working more than 100 countries around the world. Puig Chair of Global Leadership Development Leadership development is of paramount importance, especially in facing the current challenges of constant company transformation. To build sustainable organizations and maintain employee commitment and performance, human capital management strategies require leaders who adopt a long-term humanist approach, imbuing work with passion and meaning. The mission of the Puig Chair of Global Leadership Development is to help understand and apply management policies on leadership development in global companies. To this end, the Chair encourages research into effective talent management strategies that enable companies to secure both long-term economic growth and social progress through the training of responsible global leaders. We offer A professional working environment, stimulating activities in research and in-depth contact with business communities A competitive salary at the post-doc level A city that is often ranked as the most attractive European city to live in. Requirements Ph.D. degree in Organizational Behavior or related fields Demonstrated research ability excellence in the field of Organizational Behavior/Strategic Leadership; ideally, the selected candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline Profound knowledge of rigorous research methods, especially quantitative methods Recruitment procedure Interested candidates are to send: 1) a research statement, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) 2 letters of recommendations and 4) copies of 2-3 research papers"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/107601": {
      "title": "Full-time Post-Doc Position for the Juan Antonio Perez Lopez Chair at IESE Business School",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School Location: Barcelona, Spain The Post-Doc Position The Juan Antonio Perez Lopez chair at IESE Business School invites applications for a three-year Post-Doctoral position. The primary criterion for acceptance is research excellence in organizational behavior, leadership, or organization and management theory and an interest in studying topics related to corporate purpose and/or purpose-driven leadership. Ideally the candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline. The position will start in September 2022; candidates should have finished their Ph.D. degree by the start date. This position will be responsible for conducting original research with the Chairholder Prof.  John Almandoz, who will supervise the candidate’s work. The holder of this position is also expected to become actively involved in the IESE Business School intellectual communities by regularly participating in research seminars, brown bag presentations, etc. Teaching is not required. The Post-Doc Position is in Barcelona. Prof. John Almandoz will collaborate remotely from New York, and Prof. Yih-Teen Lee will help supporting the Post-Doc recipient in situ. Prof. Carlos Rey from UIC is also interested in a research collaboration involving purpose-driven organizations. Research Topics Personal and corporate purpose Purpose and positive leadership Meaningful work Institutional logics Business and society IESE Business School IESE Business School (www.iese.edu) is the Graduate School of Management of the University of Navarra, with main campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York and Sao Paulo. It offers master-level (Master in Business Administration), graduate (Ph.D. in management), and executive education programs. Founded in 1958, recent rankings of the Financial Times, the Economist, and Business Week consistently situate IESE among the top-5 business schools in Europe. With full-time professors from 25 countries and professors with PhDs from the world’s leading universities, the faculty’s teaching and research efforts are global in outlook and content. IESE has about 32.000 alumni working more than 100 countries around the world. Juan Antonio Perez Lopez Chair The Juan Antonio Perez Lopez Chair was created in 2022 to contribute to research on management and meaningful work in dialogue with the contributions of business theorist Juan Antonio Perez Lopez (1934-1996), who was a professor and dean of IESE. The focus of the Chair is to focus on research on the type of relevant questions about business in society and leadership in organizations that Juan Antonio would be asking today. We offer A professional working environment, stimulating activities in research and in-depth contact with business communities A competitive salary at the post-doc level A city that is often ranked as the most attractive European city to live in. Requirements Ph.D. degree in management, business ethics, organizational behavior, or related fields Demonstrated research ability excellence in related fields; ideally, the selected candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline Profound knowledge of rigorous research methods (experience/interest in Juan Antonio Perez Lopez is considered an advantage) Excellence in English Recruitment procedure Interested candidates are to send: 1) a research statement, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) 2 letters of recommendations and 4) copies of 2-3 research papers"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/108016": {
      "title": "Full-time Post-Doc Position for the Joaquim Molins Figueras Chair of Strategic Alliances at IESE Business School",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School Location: Barcelona, Spain IESE Business School invites applications for a Postdoctoral position with a background in strategic management or related fields, to conduct research within the Joaquim Molins Figueras Chair of Strategic Alliances. The primary criterion for acceptance is research excellence and an interest in studying topics related to strategic alliances, or broadly inter-organizational relationships. The position will start from September 2022 onwards extending up to three years. The postdoctoral researcher will work with Chairholder Prof. Africa Ariño on developing conceptual frameworks and empirical studies that extend existing theory and evidence, with the aim to publish in top outlets. While not restricted to, work on Public Private Partnerships and on cross-sector alliances is of particular interest. The position includes time dedicated to continue and publish the researcher’s ongoing research. The researcher will be subject to a formal annual performance review. The ideal candidate will be thinking of this position as a platform to build skills toward taking on a research professorship in the future.  For further information on the chair and research collaborators, please see https://www.iese.edu/faculty-research/chairs/joaquim-molins-figueras-strategic-alliances/ IESE Business School IESE Business School (www.iese.edu) is the Graduate School of Management of the University of Navarra, with main campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York, and Sao Paulo. It offers master-level (M.B.A. and Master in Management), graduate (Ph.D. in Management), and executive education programs. Founded in 1958, rankings of the Financial Times, the Economist, and Business Week consistently situate IESE among the top-5 business schools in Europe. With full-time professors from 25 countries and with PhDs from the world’s leading universities, the faculty’s research and teaching efforts are global in outlook and content. IESE has about 32,000 alumni working more than 100 countries around the world. Ph.D. degree in Management or related social science fields Demonstrated research ability excellence and enthusiasm for research to the highest quality; ideally, the selected candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline. Excellent academic record and work ethic Organizational and oral/written communication skills Profound knowledge of rigorous research methods Willingness to move and live in Barcelona (Spain). Applications should include: Cover letter including any relevant information indicating experience in research or academic work. Proof of academic qualifications and full curriculum vitae Research statement 2-3 letters of recommendations Copies of 2-3 research papers."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/115485": {
      "title": "Full-time Postdoctoral Fellow for the IESE Sustainable Leadership Initiative",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School Location: Barcelona, Spain The Sustainable Leadership Initiative (SLI) at IESE Business School invites applications for a two-year Postdoctoral fellowship. The primary criterion for acceptance is evidence of research excellence and an interest in studying sustainability-related topics. Ideally the candidate will have defended an excellent dissertation and have a strong pipeline of academic articles to be published in top academic journals. The position will start in January 2023 or as soon as possible. Candidates should have finished their PhD degree by the start date. The fellow will be responsible for conducting original research under the supervision of the Academic Director, Professor Fabrizio Ferraro, or any other of the 14 professors involved in the initiative (see website for more information).  This will help you consolidate your research pipeline and continue your academic career. You will also be involved in coordinating one international research conference on sustainable leadership, and another one targeted at corporate leaders. More broadly, it is expected that the fellow will also become actively involved in the IESE Business School intellectual communities by regularly participating in research seminars, brown bag presentations, etc. No teaching is expected or required. IESE Business School IESE Business School (www.iese.edu) is the graduate business school of the University of Navarra with campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York and Sao Paulo. It offers master’s degrees (MBA, MiM), graduate degrees (PhD in Management) and executive education. Founded in 1958, recent rankings of the Financial Times, the Economist, and Business Week consistently place IESE among the top 5 business schools in the world. With full-time professors from 25 countries and professors with PhDs from the world’s leading universities, the IESE faculty’s teaching and research efforts are global in outlook and content. IESE has more than 50,000 alumni in more than 100 countries around the world. Sustainable Leadership Initiative The IESE’s Sustainable Leadership Initiative ( https://www.iese.edu/sli ) is dedicated to generating rigorous, impactful knowledge to prompt leaders across sectors to create economic, social, and environmental value for their organizations and for society. The initiative brings together scholars and practitioners from different disciplines and aims to both foster impactful research and help diffuse it among corporate leaders and policy makers. Faculty members across the following departments are affiliated with the initiative: Accounting and Control Business Ethics Entrepreneurship Financial Management Managing People in Organizations, Operations, Information and Technology Strategic Management Research affiliated with the initiative has been published in top journals including but not limited to: Academy of Management Journal Administrative Science Quarterly Business Ethics Quarterly Journal of Accounting Research Journal of Financial Economics Management Science PhD degree in economics, sociology, strategy, management, finance, operations, etc. (any social science discipline and field in business school). Demonstrated research ability excellence in sustainability-related topics. Ideally, a strong pipeline of academic articles to be published in top academic journals (top publications a plus, but not required). Rigorous research methods expertise (either quantitative or qualitative) Interested candidates are to send the following: Research statement, specifying the fit of your research with any of the themes or professors affiliated with the SLI CV 2 letters of recommendation Copies of 2-3 research papers"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/107336": {
      "title": "Full-time Post-Doc Position for the Carl Schrøder Chair in Strategic Management at IESE Business School",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Strategic Management Location: Barcelona, Spain The Carl Schrøder chair in Strategic Management at IESE Business School invites applications for a three-year Post-Doctoral position. The primary criterion for acceptance is research excellence in management, and an interest in studying topics related to Strategy and Business Models. Ideally the candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline. The position will start in September 2022; candidates should have finished their Ph.D. degree by the start date. This position will be responsible for conducting original research with the Chairholder Prof.  Joan E. Ricart, who will supervise the candidate’s work. There is also time and room to continue research in your own pipeline. This position is also expected to become actively involved in the IESE Business School intellectual communities by regularly participating in research seminars, brown bag presentations, etc. Teaching is not required. Research Topics Governance in Sustainable Cities Business Models and Ecosystems Public-Private Collaborations in Cities IESE Business School IESE Business School (www.iese.edu) is the Graduate School of Management of the University of Navarra, with main campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York and Sao Paulo. It offers master-level (Master in Business Administration), graduate (Ph.D. in management), and executive education programs. Founded in 1958, recent rankings of the Financial Times, the Economist, and Business Week consistently situate IESE among the top-5 business schools in Europe. With full-time professors from 25 countries and professors with PhDs from the world’s leading universities, the faculty’s teaching and research efforts are global in outlook and content. IESE has about 32.000 alumni working more than 100 countries around the world. Carl Schrøder Chair: Mission and objectives The mission of the chair is the development and dissemination of knowledge in the field of strategic management. With this wide scope, the chair has focused on specific areas. Business models The phenomenon of relocation of services The new government of cities and Public-Private partnerships The deployment of the sustainable development goals Requirements Ph.D. degree in strategic management or related fields Demonstrated research ability excellence in the field of strategy and business models; ideally, the selected candidate will have some publications in top academic journals and a strong pipeline Profound knowledge of rigorous research methods Recruitment procedure Interested candidates are to send: 1) a research statement, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) 2 letters of recommendations and 4) copies of 2-3 research papers"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164649": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position at IESE",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Entrepreneurship Location: Barcelona We are excited to announce an open position for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join the Family Business Chair at IESE. The position is a full-time for two years and is expected to start in September 2025 (or by mutual agreement). The primary criterion for acceptance is research excellence in both theoretical and empirical papers, and an interest in studying topics related to family businesses and/or governance. We will accept applications on a rolling basis until April 15. Description The primary focus of this postdoc position is to develop original research in line with the chair's research agenda to publish in top management outlets. The candidate will work under the supervision of Prof. Jeroen Neckebrouck. We value the pursuit of diverse research interests that contribute to understanding of the family business/governance domain including but not limited to corporate governance and strategy, entrepreneurship and innovation, succession, strategic decision-making, human capital and human resource management, family science perspectives, role of private equity and family offices. One of the options is to assist in ongoing projects leveraging large scale administrative datasets with employee-employer matched information. More broadly, it is expected that the fellow will also become actively involved in the IESE Business School intellectual communities by regularly participating in research seminars, brown bag presentations, etc. No teaching is expected or required. The ideal candidate will be thinking of this position as a stepping stone toward taking on a research professorship in the future. PhD in management or related field (e.g. economics, finance, organizational psychology, sociology) completed or near completion Excellent academic record and work ethic. Demonstrated research ability excellence and enthusiasm for research to the highest quality Strong interest in family business and corporate governance research. Experience with large-scale datasets and advanced statistical methods is beneficial, but not mandatory. Excellent level of spoken and written English. Work-permit for Spain, and willingness to relocate to Barcelona. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. The review will begin immediately. To be considered for the position, please submit: full curriculum vitae a brief profile of your research program, including a description of theories you've used and datasets you have worked on (if applicable) and the status of current projects if possible, 2-3 letters of recommendation up to three published or working research papers"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/84953": {
      "title": "Open Rank Position in Information Systems at IESE Business School",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Information Systems Location: Barcelona, Spain The Information Systems department at IESE Business School is inviting applications for an open rank (tenure-track Assistant/ Associate/ Professor) position starting September 2020. We are looking for candidates with strong interest to develop as research- and teaching-active faculty. Depending on the stage in academic career we would like to meet candidates with: 1. a track record and potential to conduct high-quality research targeted at top tier journal outlets and 2. experience and aspiration to engage in a challenging international teaching environment at the MBA and executive levels. IESE Business School has been ranked #1 in the world for Executive Education by the Financial Times for the last five years. In addition, the school has consistently ranked among the top global MBA and Executive MBA programs. The school has campuses in Barcelona, Madrid, Munich, New York, and São Paulo. The Information Systems Department and the current position are based in Barcelona. For more information about the school, visit www.iese.edu . Research conducted by the department faculty focuses on digital innovation and digital transformation. Specific topics include the impact of digitalization on business models, digital business strategy and organizational challenges in managing digital transformation, crowdsourcing, digital entrepreneurship, organizational implications of emerging technologies (IoT, big data, blockchain), consumerization, as well as collective and artificial intelligence. We have set ambitious goals to strengthen our footprint in the research community in the upcoming years. To date, we have published in leading academic and practitioner outlets such as Management Information Systems Quarterly, Information Systems Research, Journal of the Association for Information Systems, Information and Organization, Organization Studies, Journal of Information Technology, European Journal of Information Systems, MIT Sloan Management Review, Communications of the ACM, among others. We seek individuals who can strengthen and extend the research focus of the group. The environment is highly collaborative whereas cross-departmental and interdisciplinary research projects are common and highly encouraged. For more information about the current IESE faculty and their research, see http://www.iese.edu/en/faculty-research/ Qualifications: doctorate degree in information systems and management, computer science, psychology, or related field must be completed or near completion. We also welcome applicants with a doctorate degree in any business or economics discipline if their research has a strong emphasis on digital technology and its impact on people, organizations, and markets. Application Instructions: Apply online: http://apply.interfolio.com/69737 Deadline of applications: Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three references, research statement, job market paper and further samples of your research. We will be conducting informal interviews at ICIS conference in December (15th-18th). To be considered for an informal interview at the ICIS conference, please submit a CV and contact information for three referees by November 30th. For informal inquiries, please contact Sanja Tumbas (STumbas@iese.edu) and/ or Manos Gkeredakis (MGkeredakis@iese.edu). Qualifications: doctorate degree in information systems and management, computer science, psychology, or related field must be completed or near completion. We also welcome applicants with a doctorate degree in any business or economics discipline if their research has a strong emphasis on digital technology and its impact on people, organizations, and markets. Application Instructions: Apply online: http://apply.interfolio.com/69737 Deadline of applications December 31st 2019."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/130819": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Operations Management at IESE – 2023-24",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Operations, Information and Technology Location: Barcelona, Spain IESE Business School invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions in the Operations, Information and Technology department, at the assistant or (untenured) associate levels, starting in September 2024. We are seeking candidates with a PhD in Operations Management or a related area, who are committed to excellence in research and teaching. The candidates are expected to develop a rigorous and relevant research career, with publications in leading academic journals. They must also be able to teach at the MBA level and in executive education programs. IESE is a top-rated international graduate business school with its main campuses in Barcelona and Madrid. It offers a two-year MBA program and several executive programs, both at the national and international levels, as well as a PhD program. The school has been consistently ranked among the top schools internationally, including #2 in the World in Executive Education and #3 MBA in the World by the Financial Times in 2023, as well as #1 MBA in the World by the Economist in 2021. The school has additional campuses in New York, Munich, and Sao Paulo, and offers the opportunity to teach in many different countries. IESE has a tenure system similar to the top schools in the US and salaries are competitive. In addition, the school offers excellent family policies and fringe benefits. More information about the school can be found at https://www.iese.edu . Applicants should send a research statement, a teaching statement, a curriculum vitae, copies of selected publications, three letters of recommendation, and a cover letter. All materials should be sent by September 15, 2023. Members of IESE faculty will be attending the INFORMS Annual Meeting. Therefore, candidates attending the conference are strongly encouraged to mention their attendance in their cover letter and include their presentation schedule. The department will be conducting interviews both during INFORMS and online. Please contact Ms. Noemi Jerez ( NJerez@iese.edu ) for enquiries and/or additional information. PhD in Operations Management or a related area. Research statement Teaching statement Curriculum vitae Copies of selected publications Three letters of recommendation Cover letter"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/151299": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Operations, Information and Technology at IESE – 2024-25",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Operations, Information and Technology Location: Barcelona, Spain IESE Business School invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions in the Operations, Information and Technology department, at the assistant or (untenured) associate levels, starting in September 2025. We are seeking candidates with a PhD in Operations Management, Information Systems, or a related area, who are committed to excellence in research and teaching. The candidates are expected to develop a rigorous, relevant and impactful research career, with publications in leading academic journals. Although the position is open to individuals from any research subfield and methodology, candidates working in topics related to technology, data, or in the interface of Operations Management and Information Systems are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates must also be able to teach at the master's and MBA levels and in executive education programs. IESE is a top-rated international graduate business school with its main campuses in Barcelona and Madrid. It offers a Master's in Management, a two-year MBA program, and several executive programs, both at the national and international levels, as well as a PhD program. The school has been consistently ranked among the top schools internationally, including #2 in the World in Executive Education and #3 MBA in the World by the Financial Times in 2023, as well as #1 MBA in the World by the Economist in 2021. The school has additional campuses in New York, Munich, and Sao Paulo, and offers the opportunity to teach in many different countries. IESE has a tenure system similar to the top schools in the US and salaries are competitive. In addition, the school offers excellent family policies and fringe benefits. More information about the school can be found at https://www.iese.edu . Applicants should submit a research statement, a teaching statement, a curriculum vitae, copies of selected publications, three letters of recommendation, and a cover letter. Applications will be reviewed dynamically starting on September 2, so early applications are welcome. Members of IESE faculty will be attending the INFORMS Annual Meeting in Seattle and the ICIS Conference in Bangkok. Therefore, candidates attending either of these two conferences are strongly encouraged to mention their attendance in their cover letter and include their presentation schedule. Those who plan on attending INFORMS should submit their application by September 20, while those who plan on attending ICIS should submit their application by November 8. The department will be conducting interviews both online and at those two conferences. Please contact Ms. Sònia García ( sgarcias@iese.edu ), on or after September 2, for enquiries and/or additional information. PhD in Operations Management, Information Systems, or a related area. Research statement Teaching statement Curriculum vitae Copies of selected publications Three letters of recommendation Cover letter"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171505": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Operations, Information and Technology at IESE – 2025-26",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Operations, Information and Technology Location: Madrid, Spain IESE Business School invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions in the Operations, Information and Technology department, at the assistant or (untenured) associate levels, starting in September 2026, preferably in Madrid. We are seeking candidates with a PhD in Operations Management, Information Systems, or a related area, who are committed to excellence in research and teaching. The candidates are expected to develop a rigorous, relevant and impactful research career, with publications in leading academic journals. Although the position is open to individuals from any research subfield and methodology, candidates working in topics related to technology, or in the interface of Operations Management and Information Systems are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates must also be able to teach at the master's and MBA levels and in executive education programs. IESE is a top-rated international graduate business school with its main campuses in Barcelona and Madrid. It offers a Master's in Management, a two-year MBA program, and several executive programs, both at the national and international levels, as well as a PhD program. The school has been consistently ranked among the top schools internationally, including #3 in the World in Executive Education and #3 MBA in the World by the Financial Times in 2025, as well as #1 MBA in the World by the Economist in 2021. The school has additional campuses in New York, Munich, and Sao Paulo, and offers the opportunity to teach in many different countries. IESE has a tenure system similar to the top schools in the US and salaries are competitive. In addition, the school offers excellent family policies and fringe benefits. More information about the school can be found at https://www.iese.edu . Applicants should submit a research statement, a teaching statement, a curriculum vitae, copies of selected publications, three letters of recommendation, and a cover letter. Applications will be reviewed dynamically starting on September 1, so early applications are welcome. Members of IESE faculty will be attending the INFORMS Annual Meeting in Atlanta and the ICIS Conference in Nashville. Therefore, candidates attending either of these two conferences are strongly encouraged to mention their attendance in their cover letter and include their presentation schedule. Those who plan on attending INFORMS should submit their application by September 19, while those who plan on attending ICIS should submit their application by November 6. Please contact Ms. Sònia García ( sgarcias@iese.edu ), on or after September 1, for enquiries and/or additional information. PhD in Operations Management, Information Systems, or a related area. Research statement Teaching statement Curriculum vitae Copies of selected publications Three letters of recommendation Cover letter"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/115192": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Financial Management Department",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Financial Management Department Location: Barcelona IESE’s Financial Management Department is seeking applicants for full-time, tenure-track faculty positions. We consider all levels: Assistant, Associate or full Professor. A Ph.D. in Finance or Economics by no later than September 2023 is essential. The ideal candidate will have a strong commitment to excellence in research. IESE faculty benefits from competitive resources for research, and a teaching load in line with US standards. Demonstrated ability or potential for high quality research and teaching are essential. Applicants must have a Ph.D in Finance or Economics from an accredited institution. The appointment is expected to begin on September 2023. If you are interested, please apply by November 30th 2022 through the following link, where you will also find additional information and contact details"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180651": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Position in Behavioral Decision Research",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Managerial Decision Sciences Location: IESE Business School. Barcelona, Spain The Department of Decision Sciences at IESE Business School invites applications for a postdoc position in behavioral decision research.  The postdoctoral researcher will work primarily with Professor Johannes Müller-Trede on projects in behavioral decision making and decision analysis, including experimental and analytical research on how people form judgments, make choices, and use information and advice. The position is for two years, with the possibility of an extension subject to performance and funding requirements.  It is a full-time, research-only position with independent funds for, e.g., conference travel.  The salary is competitive, and the expected start date is September 2026 (flexible). IESE Business School is one of Europe’s leading business schools, known for its international outlook, strong research infrastructure, and close connections to top institutions worldwide.  The postdoctoral researcher will be based in IESE’s Department of Decision Sciences, a leading department of its kind, and will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty within the department as well as with researchers in other departments at IESE. Barcelona is currently a major hub for behavioral research in Europe, with frequent academic events and a dense network of nearby institutions.  The city also offers an exceptional quality of life, combining a strong academic community with a rich cultural scene, Mediterranean climate, and easy access to the rest of Europe. Ideal candidates will have an interest in theoretically grounded behavioral research, as well as strong methodological training, including experience with mathematical modelling, programming, experimental design, or data analysis (in R or Python).  A PhD in decision sciences, economics, psychology, or a related field must be completed by the start date. The postdoc will be encouraged to pursue their own research agenda alongside collaborative work. Apply before March 20 th , 2026 to receive full consideration. Applications should include a CV, a sample of written work, a brief statement of research interests, and the names and contact information of two references . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For any further information, please contact: Carlota Monner ( cmonner@iese.edu )."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193916": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: IESE Business School: Managerial Decision Sciences Location: IESE Business School. Barcelona, Spain The Department of Managerial Decision Sciences at IESE Business School invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor or untenured associate professor level, starting in September 2027.  The position will initially be based at IESE’s Barcelona campus. Candidates must have completed a PhD in Decision Sciences, Economics, Statistics, Computer Science, or a related field by the start of the appointment.  They should demonstrate a record of, or strong potential for, excellence in research and teaching.  The successful candidate will be expected to develop a rigorous and impactful research program, publish in leading academic journals, and teach in both IESE’s MBA and executive education programs. IESE is an international graduate business school with a mission to develop and inspire business leaders who strive to have a deep, positive, and lasting impact on people, companies, and society through professional excellence, integrity, and a spirit of service.  In the Financial Times’ 2026 rankings, IESE ranks fourth worldwide for its MBA and third for open-enrollment executive education.  The school’s main campuses are in Barcelona and Madrid.  With additional campuses in New York, Munich, and Sao Paulo, it offers the opportunity to teach in many different countries.  IESE’s tenure system is comparable to that of leading U.S. business schools.  The school offers competitive salaries, family-friendly policies, and a range of benefits. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, selected research papers—including published or unpublished work—and three letters of recommendation through Interfolio.  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, beginning immediately.  Early applications are encouraged. Members of the department will attend the 2026 INFORMS Annual Meeting in San Francisco, November 1–4.  Candidates attending the meeting are encouraged to indicate this in their cover letter and include their presentation schedule, if applicable. Candidates seeking consideration for interviews at INFORMS are encouraged to submit their applications by October 15, 2026. Interviews will be conducted both online and at the conference. For further information, please contact Ms. Carlota Monner at cmonner@iese.edu ."
    },
    "https://jobs.iese.edu/jobs/8035992-finance-administration-manager-ny-campus": {
      "title": "Finance & Administration Manager NY Campus",
      "description": "Finance & Administration Manager NY Campus - IESE Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail New York, NY, USA · Hybrid Finance & Administration Manager NY Campus Lead finance and administrative operations in New York, overseeing budgeting, payroll, accounting, and reporting, serving employees while driving operational excellence through continuous improvement. Apply for this job Overview The Finance & Administration Manager oversees financial and administrative operations at the New York campus, including invoicing, bill payment, accounting, cash monitoring, payroll management, budgeting, reporting, and audit preparation. The person also processes employee benefits and is the first level contact for finance and HR administrative matters. The role requires professionalism, a spirit of service, and a commitment to continuous improvement. Responsibilities 1. Accounting and Financial Management Issue invoices, set up customers in their AP systems, and track collections. Process vendor payments, maintain records, review for compliance with contracts, and manage payment workflows; prepare IRS Form 1099s. Review and process employee expenses ensuring compliance with policy. Import and classify credit card transactions. Invoice or receive intercompany expenses between IESE USA and IESE Barcelona. Reconcile bank accounts and monitor cash flow. Perform monthly soft close and prepare financial reports (P&L, AR/AP, cash, year-end projections). Maintain audit-ready records and support the annual audit. 2. Budgeting and Management Control Prepare draft budgets for the annual planning cycle. Monitor results versus budget, analyze variances and report to management. Identify efficiency opportunities using financial data. Provide financial data to program and operations managers. 3. HR Administration Serve as primary contact for payroll, PTO, benefits, and HR processes. Prepare payroll submissions. Draft employment documents for approval. Maintain personnel records. Coordinate onboarding and offboarding. Ensure consistent application of HR policies. Support a professional, service-oriented work environment aligned with IESE values. Job Requirements Primarily onsite. Occasional work offsite is possible. Bachelor’s degree. Experience in accounting and financial management. HR administration experience preferred; ability to learn it on the job required. Proficiency in accounting systems and Excel; able to learn new tools. Strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and reliability. Ability to work independently and manage priorities. Service-orientation, with strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to read Spanish is a plus. Location New York, NY, USA Remote status Hybrid Employment type Full-time Apply for this job New York, NY, USA · Hybrid Finance & Administration Manager NY Campus Lead finance and administrative operations in New York, overseeing budgeting, payroll, accounting, and reporting, serving employees while driving operational excellence through continuous improvement. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    }
